@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox
title UC-FM03 — one independently authorized section read
actor Family
boundary "FamilyVisitProgressPage\nuseFamilyVisitProgress" as Page
control "Spring Security\nSession / role" as Security
control VisitController as Controller
control "FamilyVisit{Detail,Timeline,Task}Service" as Service
control FamilyReadAudit as Audit
control FamilyAccessQuery as Access
entity "VisitRepository +\nsection repository" as Repos
database "MySQL" as DB

Family -> Page : View progress (visitId)
Page -> Security : GET /api/auth/me
Security --> Page : Current account and roles
note over Page
A changed account clears prior data.
Only a confirmed FAMILY session starts the three GETs.
Session failure skips section reads and follows error handling.
end note
loop details / timeline / tasks (parallel requests; no shared snapshot)
  Page -> Security : GET /api/visits/{id}[/timeline|/tasks]
  alt Session or role rejected
    Security --> Page : 401 / 403; no protected content
  else Allowed into FAMILY branch
    Security -> Controller : Authenticated username and visitId
    Controller -> Service : findDetail / findTimeline / findTasks
    Service -> Audit : read(username, resource, visitId, query)
    Audit -> Repos : query callback: findById(visitId)
    Repos -> DB : Read visit
    DB --> Repos : Saved visit (or missing)
    Repos --> Audit : Visit facts
    alt Visit missing
      Audit -> Audit : Query fails with ResourceNotFound
    else Visit exists
    Audit -> Access : requireReadableElder(username, visit.elderId)
    Access -> DB : Current user/profile and effective binding
    DB --> Access : Authorization facts
    Access --> Audit : Allow or deny
    opt Authorized section needs child records
      Audit -> Repos : findAppliedByVisitId / findByVisitId
      Repos -> DB : Read ordered saved records
      DB --> Repos : APPLIED transitions / tasks
      Repos --> Audit : Section data
    end
    end
    Audit -> DB : Persist READ audit via AccessAudit
    alt Audit unavailable
      Audit --> Page : 503 without section content
    else Audit persisted
      Audit --> Service : Data or rethrow query failure
      Service --> Controller : Result or 403 / 404
      Controller --> Page : Family DTO or error
    end
  end
end
note over Page
Details: server asOf. Child arrays: client loadedAt.
Success updates only its section; retryable failure keeps stale prior data.
Any 400/401/403/404 clears all sections and stops polling.
Visible + online: next round 15s after completion; failure 30/60s.
Manual retry, pause/resume and cleanup are in the activity diagram.
end note
@enduml
